Z||000000||Haze_Performance||07-06-2000||03:32 PM||||fierodan   posted 02-02-2000 03:58 PM ET (US)             <BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>When I was working at Rockford Fosgate down in Arizona as a tech, I managed to fit two Power series 15" subs up front in an isobaric bandpass enclosure....and fitted a Power 1100a2 to it that was pushing 1439 watts. I had to cut out much of the metal, the washer tank, the AC canister and all of the plastic........but it's been done. =)<BR>Dan<P>2 15"s in a Fiero!?!?!?!?!?<P>goto  <A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com/ubb/Forum1/HTML/000008.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.v8archie.com/ubb/Forum1/HTML/000008.html</A> <BR> <P>------------------<BR>Carl (85 Fiero) My Website's  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/HMP" TARGET=_blank>Haze Mustang Performance</A>   &  <A HREF="http://www.drive.to/WS6_Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>WS6 Fiero</A>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Homicidal||07-06-2000||03:52 PM||||Very much so!  BUT, they air space it had would't sound good on the sub part.  Probably 1 10" or 12" sub in a great big enclosure sounds equal to those two 15's.  <P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ironhorse||07-07-2000||04:32 PM||||hey Haze.  YOu gotta send me a detail instruction on how you do that and also gimme some pix of hte install.<P>I plan on installing a mtx5000 15 inch under the passenger dash in F-15 (name of my 85gt).<BR>Everybody in my town says that it can't be done. They also said that I wouldn't fit in a fiero 6'ft tall 300lb, wear 46 pant, I get in and out juuuust fine.  I'm planning on installing MTX- 2 275, 1 2300, 1 mtx5000 15, 2 mtx5000 8 inch, 2 kicker 61/2, 1 eslipse 2101 xover/linedriver/equalizer, 1 sony or kenwood cdplayer.    I'm gonna have a tiny n loud F15.  I know I can do it, but as far as 15 inch I would like to try to do it without cuttin... it require 1.5 cu ft airspace.||||reg||1
Z||000003||stimpy||07-07-2000||10:28 PM||||Ironhorse...about that 15 under the dash. I might suggest scaling back to a 10. A 10 will fit straight up and down under the vent ducting, and an enclosure that fits flush with the "footrest" has enough air space for a good "low Q" speaker. I'm running a Polk dX10 and itsounds great. Right now I don't have nearly enough power to really test it, but it turns my rearview into a blur nonetheless. <BR>Just my 2 cents, would be interested in seeing how you hook all that up if you go ahead and do all that.  <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://gifs123.tripod.com/page15/renstimpy2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||stillofknight||07-09-2000||08:15 PM||||You guys ever consider the new L7 Solobarics from Kicker?  They are kind of expensive, but they are easier to mount, and they fit in a tiny enclosure.||||reg||1
